--- Project-specific guidance for mock3 ---

This phase covers two stories across two codelines, both small boundary/off-by-one fixes in TypeScript exercised by vitest:

- MOCK3-1 (mocka, /home/bradleyjerome/projects/mock3/mock-a): Riders aged exactly 65 must be charged the adult fare. The fix touches fareFor / totalFor. When classifying criteria, pay close attention to whether the diff and test evidence cover the exact boundary value of age 65 — not just ages above or below it. The mocka-investigator role was responsible for confirming no caller of fareFor or totalFor relies on the current incorrect boundary and for characterising what test coverage for age 65 should look like; expect their findings in the injected evidence.

- MOCK3-2 (mockb, /home/bradleyjerome/projects/mock3/mock-b): The departure board omits the final stop. The fix touches formatStops. When classifying criteria, verify that the diff and test evidence demonstrate the last stop is now included in the rendered output — not merely that the loop runs one iteration further. The mockb-investigator role was responsible for verifying no caller compensates for the missing last stop and for describing what the test suite currently asserts about stop rendering; expect their findings in the injected evidence.

The implementer role typescript-bugfix-engineer spanned both codelines, so implementation evidence for both stories may appear in a single diff or commit set.

Both codelines depend on vitest and typescript. Do not infer build or test commands beyond what the injected evidence provides; classify based solely on the pre-injected diff, test oracle, and story oracle.
